TomTom's map is seen by millions of people every day - in dashboards, on phones, and across partner products worldwide. As a Senior UX Designer on the Map Visualisation team, you will shape how our 2D and 3D geospatial data is designed, styled and delivered across TomTom's product portfolio.&nbsp;


You'll spend your days crafting multi-zoom map experiences, working with spatial data and collaborating closely with engineers and product managers to turn cartographic intent into production-ready map styles. You'll need to be as comfortable discussing label collision and style-layer specifications with engineers as you are refining colour palettes and visual hierarchy.&nbsp;


This is a product role first. You'll be embedded in a cross-functional team that ships map rendering, map styles and SDKs used by other TomTom products and by the customers who build on our platform. You'll take part in the whole development lifecycle, from discovery and solution design through pull requests to release. Your product judgement, and your ability to bring people with competing priorities to a clear decision, matter here as much as your cartographic craft.&nbsp;


AI is part of how we work. We expect you to use it to explore, prototype and ship faster, to know where it falls short, and to help shape map experiences in products where AI is part of the experience itself.&nbsp;
What You'll Do 



Design Compelling Map Experiences Create and refine 2D and 3D map visualisations from concept through production delivery. Own the end-to-end cartographic design process - from data exploration and sketching through to style implementation, QA and iteration across zoom levels, regions and use cases.&nbsp;






Maintain and Evolve Core Map Styles Enhance TomTom's core map styles, ensuring consistency, readability and visual quality across platforms, screen densities and global markets. Balance aesthetic ambition with rendering performance and data constraints.&nbsp;






Work as Part of the Product Team Work day-to-day alongside software engineers and product managers building TomTom's map data structures, renderers and SDKs. Take part in planning, refinement and reviews, provide design specifications engineers can act on, and review visual output during development and before release.&nbsp;






Make and Own Trade-offs Help decide what ships, when and at what quality. Weigh visual fidelity against render budget, memory and frame rate on automotive and mobile hardware, customer requests against platform consistency, and scope against release dates. Reach a decision with the people who own the product, record it and see it through.&nbsp;






Contribute to Renderer and Tooling Requirements Provide detailed input on the data and rendering capabilities needed to achieve design goals. Define requirements for internal cartographic authoring tools and identify workflow improvements that raise the team's output quality and speed.&nbsp;






Bring AI into the Design Workflow Use AI to shorten the loop from idea to rendered map: generating and editing style-spec JSON, scripting data exploration, and building interactive prototypes on real data instead of static frames. Turn what works into shared workflows the team can reuse, and help define how we check AI-generated output for cartographic quality.&nbsp;






Design for AI-Driven Map Experiences Contribute to how the map responds when the request comes from an AI system rather than a tap, for example in GeoAI answers, conversational search or agent-generated routes. Work out how the map shows what the AI found, how confident it is and when it is wrong.&nbsp;






Inform Decisions with Research and Data Participate in user research, customer conversations and competitive benchmarking. Use insights to ground design decisions and advocate for improvements that address real user needs.&nbsp;






Support the Design System and Standards Contribute to the Map Visualisation design system - documenting patterns, conventions and cartographic guidelines that enable consistency and scale across the product portfolio.&nbsp;



What You'll Need 

Leadership &amp; Product Team Experience&nbsp;




A track record of shaping product direction from the design seat. You set out the options, make the case for one and bring engineering, product and business stakeholders with you.&nbsp;






A track record of shipping software as a designer embedded in a product team, ideally on map, location or developer-platform products: SDKs, APIs, map styles or tooling that other teams and companies build on.&nbsp;








A clear understanding of how products move from discovery to release and beyond, including planning, roadmaps and measuring results after launch. You know how versioned releases, deprecations and backwards compatibility shape design choices on a platform with external customers.&nbsp;






Hands-on familiarity with how software gets built: backlogs, refinement, estimation, definition of done, Git, pull requests, code reviews, CI/CD, feature flags and release trains. You don't need to write production code, but you need to understand how your designs move through a rendering pipeline and into a release.&nbsp;






Sound judgement under constraint. You can point to decisions where you gave something up to ship, and explain why it was right for the product and its users.&nbsp;






Clarity with senior audiences. You can turn a complex design problem into a short, well-argued recommendation and own the result.&nbsp;






Comfort with disagreement. You challenge a decision with evidence, accept the outcome when it goes the other way and keep the work moving.&nbsp;






Experience contributing to solution design documents, technical specifications and cross-functional planning.&nbsp;




Cartography &amp; Digital Map Making&nbsp;




A solid foundation in digital cartography, GIS or geographic information design. If your map-making depth is still growing, show us how fast you are closing the gap, including how you use AI to learn.&nbsp;






Experience designing multi-zoom digital maps with attention to cartographic conventions, label placement, generalisation and cultural adaptation.&nbsp;






Working proficiency with key mapping technologies and ecosystems: MapLibre, Mapbox GL JS, OpenStreetMap data and tooling, QGIS, ArcGIS, Leaflet, OpenLayers or comparable platforms.&nbsp;






Experience working with diverse spatial datasets - vector tiles, raster tiles, GeoJSON, shapefiles, point clouds or terrain data.&nbsp;






Awareness of cartographic standards across regions and cultures, including sensitive topics such as disputed borders and local place names.&nbsp;




Map Visualisation &amp; Rendering&nbsp;




Demonstrated ability to build visually compelling 2D and 3D map experiences - from thematic styling and terrain visualisation to street-level detail.&nbsp;






Hands-on experience designing 3D map content such as buildings, terrain, landmarks and lane-level road geometry, in stylised or realistic form. You understand how LOD, lighting, materials and camera pitch affect legibility and performance.&nbsp;






Experience with 3D data formats and pipelines such as glTF and 3D Tiles, and how 3D assets are prepared and optimised for real-time map rendering.&nbsp;






Good understanding of real-time rendering concepts as they apply to maps: style layers, zoom interpolation, data-driven styling, symbol rendering and performance considerations.&nbsp;




AI in Your Practice&nbsp;




Evidence that AI has changed how you work. Be ready to show a real example, such as a map style, data visualisation or coded prototype built with AI, and tell us where it let you down.&nbsp;






Sharp judgement of AI output. You can spot errors in generated work and know which decisions still need a designer's eye.&nbsp;








Experience turning personal AI use into workflows the team shares, within the limits of confidential data and licensing.&nbsp;




Senior-Level Craft &amp; Collaboration&nbsp;




5+ years of professional experience in UX, product or cartographic design, with most of that time spent inside software product teams.&nbsp;






Bachelor's or Master's degree in Cartography, Geography, GIS, UX Design, Computer Science or a related field - or equivalent professional experience.&nbsp;






Ability to build clear, concise prototypes and specification documentation that bridge design and engineering.&nbsp;






Strong visual and graphic design fundamentals - typography, colour theory, hierarchy and layout.&nbsp;






User-centric mindset with a collaborative, low-ego approach to problem-solving.&nbsp;






High attention to detail and a real passion for the craft of map making.&nbsp;



Nice to Have 



Experience with game engines or 3D content pipelines (Unity, Unreal Engine, Blender) and their application to geospatial visualisation.&nbsp;






Familiarity with front-end languages and graphics APIs (JavaScript/TypeScript, WebGL, WebGPU, GLSL) or scripting for cartographic automation (Python, PostGIS, Overpass API). With AI, even basic coding skills go a long way.&nbsp;






Experience with map data processing tools and pipelines: Tippecanoe, Tilemaker, osm2pgsql, Mapnik or similar.&nbsp;






Understanding of the automotive, fleet management or logistics industries and their mapping requirements.&nbsp;






Familiarity with emerging trends in spatial computing, AR navigation or digital twins.&nbsp;






Experience contributing to design systems at scale.&nbsp;



What we offer A competitive compensation package, of course. &nbsp;Time and resources to grow and develop, including a personal development budget and paid leave for learning days, as well as paid access to e-learning resources such as O’Reilly and LinkedIn Learning.&nbsp;Time to support life outside of work, with enhanced parental leave plus paid leave to care for loved ones and volunteer in local communities.&nbsp;&nbsp;Work flexibility, where TomTom’ers, in agreement with their manager and team, use both the office and home to focus, collaborate, learn and socialize. It’s all about getting the best out of both worlds –&nbsp;we ask TomTom’ers to come to the office two days a week, and the remaining three are free to be worked in either location.Improve your home office with a setup budget and get extra support with a monthly allowance.&nbsp;Enjoy options to work from your home country and abroad for a set number of days each year, to visit family and friends, or to simply explore the world we’re mapping. &nbsp;Take the holidays you want with a competitive holiday plan, plus an extra day off to celebrate your birthday.&nbsp;Join annual events like our      Hackathon and DevDays to bring your ideas to life with talented teammates from around the world.&nbsp;Become a part of our inclusive global culture and have the chance to collaborate with a diverse community – we have over 80 nationalities at TomTom!&nbsp;Find out more about&nbsp;our global benefits and enjoy additional local benefits tailored to your location.&nbsp;Meet your teamWe’re the User Experience Design team. Fueled by user insights and data analytics, our mission is to create powerful, easy-to-use products that delight our customers, from millions of drivers to automotive customers who embed our technologies in their vehicles. We deliver the design specifications for all TomTom’s products. Joining us, you'll be part of a team that brings together design disciplines from user research to interaction, concept and visual design. Together, we'll continue to develop a map that people trust all around the world.  At TomTom...You’ll help people find their way in the world. In 2004, TomTom revolutionized how the world moves with the introduction of the first portable navigation device. Now, we intend to do it again by engineering the first-ever real-time map, the smartest and most useful map on the planet.Work with a team of 3,600+ unique, curious and passionate problem-solvers. Together, we’ll open up a world of possibilities for car manufacturers, enterprises and developers to help people understand and get closer to the world around them.After you applyOur recruitment team will work hard to give you a meaningful experience throughout your journey with us, no matter the outcome. Your application will be screened closely and you can rest assured that all follow-up actions will be thorough, from assessments and interviews all the way through onboarding. To find out more about our application process, check out our hiring FAQs.TomTom is an equal opportunity employerTomTom is where you can find your place in the world. Every day we welcome, nurture and celebrate differences. Why? Because your uniqueness is what makes you, you. No matter your culture or background, you’ll find your impact at TomTom.&nbsp;Research also shows that sometimes women and underrepresented communities can be hesitant to apply for positions unless they believe they meet 100% of the criteria. If you can relate to this, please know that we’d love to hear from you.Find more English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What is Contentstack?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contentstack is redefining how modern digital experiences are built and managed. As the pioneer of the Agentic Experience Platform (AXP), Contentstack brings together structured content and brand governance (Content Cloud), real-time customer data, omnichannel personalization (Data Cloud) and autonomous AI orchestration (Agent OS) into one unified system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While many organizations adopted headless CMS or standalone AI tools expecting transformation, they often found themselves managing disconnected systems and manual workflows. Contentstack helps enterprises move beyond that complexity by connecting content, data and AI in a way that makes digital experiences faster to launch, easier to manage and more adaptive in real time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leading brands including Steve Madden, LG Electronics, Subaru of America, Dolce &amp;amp; Gabbana, ASICS, Decathlon, and Caesars Entertainment rely on Contentstack to reduce operational friction and deliver personalized, scalable digital experiences with confidence. The company is known for its customer-first culture and commitment to the communities it serves through the Contentstack Cares program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--focus-visible&quot; href=&quot;http://www.contentstack.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://www.contentstack.com&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;www.contentstack.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Contentstack we are more than colleagues, we are a tribe. Our vision is to pursue equity among our communities, employees, partners, and customers. We are global-diverse yet close; distributed yet connected. We are dreamers and dreammakers who challenge the status quo. We do the right thing, even when no one is watching. We are curious trendspotters and brave trendsetters. Our mission is to make Contentstack indispensable for organizations to tell their stories and to connect with the people they care about through inspiring, modern experiences. We care deeply about our customers and the communities we serve. #OneTeamOneDream. Chalo, let’s go!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;What Are We Looking For?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Business Intelligence Data Architect&lt;/strong&gt; to shape the analytical architecture, data modeling standards, and engineering practices that power enterprise reporting, governed metrics, and AI-enabled analytics at Contentstack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this high-impact role, you’ll establish scalable, reusable modeling frameworks across Snowflake and dbt, lead the implementation of governed semantic models, and partner with Data Engineering, BI &amp;amp; Analytics, Revenue Operations, Finance, and executive leadership to build a trusted foundation for data-driven decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re passionate about modern analytics architecture, translating complex business needs into scalable solutions, and enabling the next generation of AI-powered analytics, we’d love to hear from you! Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead analytical architecture and governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Define enterprise modeling standards across staging, intermediate, dimensional, fact, semantic, and mart layers. Establish conventions for model grain, naming, ownership, lineage, and documentation, and lead architectural design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build governed data models and semantic layers:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement reusable business entities, semantic models, and enterprise metrics that support consistent reporting, self-service analytics, applications, and AI-enabled workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish analytics engineering best practices:&lt;/strong&gt; Set standards for dbt development, testing, Git workflows, CI/CD, deployment reliability, model performance, and observability to improve scalability and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable secure, reliable data access:&lt;/strong&gt; Design governed access patterns for applications, AI agents, and self-service tools consuming Snowflake data, including role-based access control (RBAC), APIs, service layers, and query optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across the business:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Data Engineering, BI &amp;amp; Analytics, Revenue Operations, Finance, and executive stakeholders to translate business requirements into trustworthy data models and scalable analytics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor and enable the team:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide analytics engineers on modular architecture, semantic implementation, reusable modeling patterns, and modern analytics engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive platform evolution:&lt;/strong&gt; Evaluate tools, semantic technologies, governance capabilities, and architectural improvements that support long-term scalability while reducing technical debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;What Really Gets Us Excited About You&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-8 years of experience in data engineering, analytics engineering, or data architecture, including at least 3 years in an architect capacity with direct ownership of an analytical platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise in Snowflake architecture, including virtual warehouse design, RBAC, materialization strategies, dynamic tables, and query performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level experience with dbt, including staging/intermediate/mart conventions, Jinja macros, incremental models, testing, documentation, and reusable modeling patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of dimensional and semantic modeling, with the ability to select and justify approaches based on business and analytical needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing and deploying production semantic layers and governed metrics across BI platforms, analytics applications, and AI-enabled workflows, including text-to-SQL and MCP-based integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL skills and experience with Python, along with familiarity with dbt Cloud, Fivetran, Git, CI/CD, and cloud-native analytics environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing secure data access patterns for applications consuming Snowflake data, including APIs, service layers, RBAC, query performance, and governed semantic access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain architectural decisions to technical teams, executive leaders, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with globally distributed teams across the US, Europe, and India.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snowflake SnowPro Core or Advanced certification; dbt Certified Data Architect or Analytics Engineer certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Snowflake Cortex and Snowpark ML for in-warehouse AI/ML workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Salesforce as a source system, including dimensional modeling for go-to-market (GTM) data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) architectures that connect large language models to governed analytical data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with BI tools such as Tableau, Looker, or Power BI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing data governance frameworks, including data catalogs, column-level lineage, and row-level security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value a fun, collaborative, and innovative culture!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Do We Offer?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interesting Work |&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We hire curious trendspotters and brave trendsetters. This is NOT your boring, routine, cushy, rest-and-vest corporate job. This is the “challenge yourself” role where you learn something new every day, never stop growing, and have fun while you’re doing it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tribe Vibe &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;| We are more than colleagues, we are a tribe. We have a strict “no a**hole policy” and enforce it diligently. This means we spend time together - with spontaneous office happy hours, organized outings, and community volunteer opportunities. We are a diverse and distributed team, but we like to stay connected.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bragging Rights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; |&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; We are dreamers and dream makers. Our efforts pay off and we work with the most prestigious brands, from big-name retailers to airlines, to professional sports teams. Your contribution will make an impact with many of the most recognizable names in almost every industry including AirFrance KLM, ASICS, Burberry, Mattel, Mitsubishi, Walmart, and many more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One Team One Dream &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; This is one of our values, and it shows. We don’t believe in artificial hierarchies. If you’re part of the tribe, you have an opportunity to contribute. Your voice will be heard and you will also receive regular updates about the business and its performance. Which, btw, is through the roof, so it’s a great time to be joining…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;To review our Privacy Policy, please click &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.contentstack.com/legal/privacy-notice-for-candidates/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Engineer II to join our Platform squad working on one of Hudl’s most innovative products: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/en_gb/products/focus&quot;&gt;next-generation, fully automated sports cameras&lt;/a&gt;. These autonomous cameras use edge AI to automatically track the action and upload to the cloud, giving our customers seamless access to vital, real-time video and insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform squad builds the foundation our hardware teams rely on - the build systems, tooling, update pipeline and security processes that take our cameras from development through manufacturing and into the field. As we bring up our next-generation hardware platform, you’ll help shape how it’s built, tested, shipped and kept secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineer II, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support our hardware squads.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll help hardware squads integrate their work into our CI/CD pipelines, so every change is built, tested and delivered reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build development tools.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll create and improve the tools our engineers use every day to build, flash, debug and test devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep our infrastructure running.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll maintain our CI/CD infrastructure, including the regression testing that runs in manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship updates to the field.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll roll out software updates to our customers’ cameras safely and predictably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable manufacturing.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll provide the tooling our contract manufacturers use to flash, provision and test devices on the production line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the problem.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll work in an autonomous squad that has the freedom and expertise to deliver the best solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We’re currently considering applicants within commuting distance of Den Bosch. You’ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yocto experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked with Yocto and are comfortable building and customizing images.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD know-how.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve built or maintained CI/CD pipelines (for example, GitHub Actions, GitLab or Jenkins), including build automation and automated testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scripting and tooling skills.&lt;/strong&gt; You write clean, maintainable tools and automation in Bash and Python, and you’re comfortable with Docker and Linux system administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable withAI-assisted development.&lt;/strong&gt; You work fluently with AI coding tools and can evaluate their output critically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OTA update experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked with over-the-air update frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manufacturing experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve built flashing, provisioning or end-of-line test tooling for production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embedded platform experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked with SoC vendor BSPs, flashing tools or secure boot on platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Low-level development.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re comfortable reading and debugging C/C++ code, from user space down to kernel drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security vulnerability management.&lt;/strong&gt; You have experience identifying, triaging and resolving security vulnerabilities in embedded Linux systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony&lt;/strong&gt;. We’ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time above any required statutory leave, company-wide holidays, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too.&amp;nbsp; Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;. We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you’ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth. &lt;/strong&gt;We’re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We’ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed&lt;/strong&gt;. We&#39;ve invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you’re at the office or working remotely, we’ll provide you the tech you need to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing. &lt;/strong&gt;Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you’re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is displayed below—&lt;strong&gt;starting salaries will typically fall near the middle of this range.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make compensation decisions based on an individual&#39;s experience, skills and education in line with our internal pay equity practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€51.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€85.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

Finom is a fast-growing European tech startup, headquartered in Amsterdam, on a mission to revolutionize the financial landscape for entrepreneurs globally. We are developing an all-in-one financial B2B solution that seamlessly integrates banking functions, accounting, financial management, and invoicing into a mobile-first platform.
&nbsp;
Following a significant €115 million Series C equity round, bringing our total funding to approximately $346 million, we are expanding aggressively across key EU markets (Germany, France, Netherlands, Italy, Spain). We go beyond traditional banking, offering invoicing and a growing suite of features, including AI-enabled accounting, to simplify financial management for small and medium-sized businesses.
&nbsp;
At Finom, we empower our employees to make a real difference. We nurture an innovative and inspiring environment where bold ideas thrive, prioritizing thorough research, swift implementation, and ensuring every effort benefits our users, partners, and our business as a whole.
&nbsp;
Engineering Manager - Product
&nbsp;
We're looking for an Engineering Manager who's both a technical leader and a product builder. You'll guide a cross-functional team (5-10 engineers across backend, frontend, mobile, and QA) in delivering products that create real value for hundreds of thousands of businesses across Europe.What You Will Be Doing
You're a seasoned technical leader with strong engineering roots and a track record of building teams that ship products that matter. You communicate clearly with everyone – engineers, product managers, executives – and you're genuinely curious about the product, the users, the business, and how your team's work drives real impact.
You don't just manage delivery. You challenge problem framing with your PM partner, ensure the team solves the right problems, and think in terms of business outcomes, not just technical outputs. You're comfortable discussing retention and conversion funnels alongside system architecture. You help the team understand ROI and prioritize based on value and effort.
You have deep technical expertise and can still step in to unblock when needed. You balance feature delivery with technical debt, keeping scalability in mind while ensuring the team ships at pace. You make technical decisions through explicit trade-offs, not gut feelings, and help everyone understand the "why" behind choices.
You take ownership of both outcomes and people. You run meaningful 1:1s, create growth plans, and own hiring and promotions. You build engaged teams through honest feedback and coaching. You invest in making the team more productive – better tools, smarter processes, fewer bottlenecks.
You drive predictable delivery by partnering tightly with Product and Design. You communicate proactively about priorities, risks, and constraints. You encourage healthy debate and move toward "disagree and commit" when needed.
Who You Are
5+ years of software development building data-intensive production systems
Proven track record leading cross-functional engineering teams
Deep technical knowledge: hands-on experience with at least one of the common general-purpose languages and platforms (C#/.NET, Java/JVM, JavaScript/Node, Go), distributed architectures, databases, messaging and queueing systems.
Experience in product-led organizations, ideally with international scopeStrong business acumen – you connect engineering work to revenue, retention, and trust
Comfortable with product metrics (DAU/MAU, retention, conversion funnels)
Exceptional communication in English across all audiencesA builder's mentality: you care about shipping great products and growing great teams
Our tech stack&nbsp;


Backend: .NET Core, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, Kafka, Kubernetes


You'll lead teams using React, Swift/Kotlin, Python/ML frameworks, and modern QA tools

What You Will Get In Return
&nbsp;
Make a genuine impact on the product
&nbsp;
We're a growing fintech serving hundreds of thousands of European businesses. You'll lead a domain team with real ownership and autonomy over what you build and how you build it. This is a place for curious leaders who want to grow as technical managers, product thinkers, and people leaders.
&nbsp;
Work in the EU
&nbsp;
Embark on this exciting journey with us and enjoy the flexibility of traveling and working remotely or in a hybrid model across Europe.
&nbsp;
Become a stock options holder
&nbsp;
Unlock your inner entrepreneur and align your aspirations with ours through our Stock Options Program. This exciting opportunity is available to every team member, from junior team members to our founders.
&nbsp;
Receive unwavering support and care
&nbsp;
Finom stands by you at every step, embodying our commitment to your well-being and success reflected in our modern, friendly, and eco-conscious corporate culture. We offer constant support and care to ensure your Finom experience is successful and fulfilling.
&nbsp;
Work &amp; Swim program
&nbsp;
Immerse yourself in our exclusive Work &amp; Swim Program. Spend one month in a comfortable corporate apartment in enchanting Cyprus. It's the ideal opportunity to strike the perfect work-life balance while enjoying breathtaking Mediterranean views.
&nbsp;
Equal Opportunity Statement&nbsp;
&nbsp;
At Finom, we're an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We embrace diversity and invite applications from all walks of life. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, disability status, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.Find Jobs in Netherlands on Arbeitnow

Are you a budding software enthusiast with a passion for innovation and a knack for problem-solving? Do you dream of building applications that truly make a difference, collaborating with a diverse team, and shaping the future of software development?
If so, we'd love for you to join us at Mendix (a Siemens Company)!&nbsp;


About&nbsp;Mendix: The Leading Low-Code Application Development Platform&nbsp;


The software development industry is evolving, moving away from traditional approaches towards AI-assisted platforms that make building applications faster and smarter. Unlike traditional programming languages, where business logic can quickly become buried in layers of code,&nbsp;Mendix&nbsp;provides everyone involved in&nbsp;development&nbsp;a clear, visual understanding of what is&nbsp;being&nbsp;built. This approach enables&nbsp;business people, analysts, web developers, software engineers, and even CEOs to&nbsp;participate&nbsp;significantly, thereby creating better applications faster.&nbsp;


The&nbsp;Mendix&nbsp;Platform uses visual modeling to abstract long-form&nbsp;coding out of&nbsp;application development. Our customers use&nbsp;Mendix&nbsp;to create and deploy better software for the enterprise, faster.&nbsp;Mendix&nbsp;enables collaboration between business users and developers to work together throughout the development process. Read our Customer Stories to learn more about the wealth of software and solutions global organizations have built with the Platform.&nbsp;


At&nbsp;Mendix, we strive to&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;a diverse, open, and safe working environment where people can be their true selves. We value every voice, celebrate individuality, and appreciate the diversity of thought and experience.&nbsp;People who work here are driven, smart, and&nbsp;really good&nbsp;at what they do.&nbsp;As this market evolves, we encourage people of all skill levels to work with the platform, both for clients and candidates.&nbsp;

Join Our Team!&nbsp;


As part of our organization, you will help build Mendix, an application development platform that empowers technical and non-technical developers. Your work will have a direct impact on improving the productivity and ability to innovate of the development community. You will help us build a future where applications are built with collaboration across organizations. This is an exciting opportunity to kickstart your career in a dynamic and forward-thinking environment.


You're the Software Engineer We're Looking for If: 



You show clear proficiency in at least one programming language like&nbsp; TypeScript, React and C# a bonus.&nbsp;






You know how to use AI&nbsp;assisted&nbsp;development tooling to improve development speed and quality.&nbsp;

You have at least 3 years software development experience.
You have graduated in Software Engineering or a similar program.&nbsp;





You&nbsp;possess&nbsp;a genuine passion for technology and strong problem-solving and analytical skills.&nbsp;






You're&nbsp;adept at breaking down challenges and constructing solutions with short feedback cycles.&nbsp;






You take ownership of your work and are committed to helping your team succeed.&nbsp;






You thrive in a team environment, building innovative software.&nbsp;



What's In It For You? 


We believe in supporting our team members both professionally and personally. Here’s a glimpse of the fantastic benefits you can expect:&nbsp;




Competitive Salary: Enjoy a competitive salary with regular reviews and opportunities for advancement.&nbsp;






Generous Time Off: Recharge with&nbsp;30 days&nbsp;of Paid Time Off (PTO).&nbsp;






Flexible Work: Benefit from our hybrid work environment and the option to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year.&nbsp;








Career Growth: Access&nbsp;career&nbsp;development training and opportunities, along with a dedicated training budget for professional development.&nbsp;






Team Fun: Participate&nbsp;in regular team events and outings like escape rooms and carting – because collaboration extends beyond the office!&nbsp;






Delicious Perks: Enjoy&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;daily lunch at the office.&nbsp;






Work-Life Balance: Take advantage of flexible working hours to accommodate a healthy work-life balance.&nbsp;






Commute Support: Various modes of travel to and from the office are covered by&nbsp;Mendix.&nbsp;






Innovation Time: Get creative with 2 crafting days per month.&nbsp;




Why Siemens?

At Siemens, we are committed to fostering an environment where our employees can thrive and make a significant impact. We offer:&nbsp;




Innovative Technology: Contribute to a leading low-code platform that is transforming industries globally.&nbsp;






Meaningful Work: The opportunity to directly influence customer success and contribute to a product that delivers tangible value.&nbsp;






Professional Development: A culture that promotes continuous learning, professional growth, and staying abreast of technological advancements.&nbsp;






Collaborative Environment: A supportive, agile, and inclusive team where contributions are valued, and collaboration is integral.&nbsp;




Comprehensive Benefits: The salary range for this position is €59.100 to 91.800 annually. The actual compensation offered is based on the&nbsp;successful candidate’s job-related skills, experience, and relevant education/training. Siemens offers health and wellness benefits to employees; you can access the benefits&nbsp;


available in your country via the link:&nbsp;Benefits | Siemens Digital Industries Software&nbsp;


Join Our Team!&nbsp;


We invite qualified candidates to apply for this challenging and rewarding opportunity to contribute to a world-class team.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
