You’ll be confident working independently and ready to take on a senior role within the team. Alongside your clinical work, you’ll have genuine scope to help shape the future of our farm service, providing clinical leadership, supporting colleagues and helping to bring further structure and development to the service.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
What You’ll Be Stepping Into
&nbsp;
This role is available on a rota of between 25 ad 36 hours a week (part time or full time), with an on-call commitment of one weeknight and one in four weekends for farm or mixed work depending on your requirements and circumstances.
&nbsp;
The role offers a varied farm only or mixed caseload, depending on your experience and interests, alongside the opportunity to contribute at a more senior level. We are also happy to be flexible with hours and rota patterns for the right candidate.
&nbsp;
You’ll play an important part in the ongoing development of the farm service, working closely with the team to provide clinical support, leadership and structure. We’re looking for someone who is confident making decisions independently and who enjoys sharing their knowledge and experience with colleagues.
&nbsp;
