The Team &amp; Facilities
&nbsp;
You’ll be joining a supportive, forward-thinking team with a strong focus on delivering high-quality clinical care while maintaining a positive working environment. This is an opportunity to work alongside colleagues who value collaboration and clinical support, while giving you the autonomy to bring your own experience and ideas to the role.
&nbsp;
As a senior member of the farm team, you’ll have the opportunity to influence how the service develops and help create greater structure and consistency across the farm offering. Whether you come from a predominantly farm background or are a mixed vet looking to focus more heavily on farm work, there is plenty of scope to make the position your own.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Location &amp; Culture
&nbsp;
Based at Border Vets in Longtown, this role offers the opportunity to work within a well-established veterinary team while enjoying the benefits of a genuinely part-time working pattern.
&nbsp;
We understand that a senior veterinary role doesn’t have to mean giving up your work-life balance. With three working days per week and a clearly defined on-call commitment, this could be an ideal opportunity for an experienced vet looking for greater responsibility and influence without stepping into a full-time role.
&nbsp;
If you’re an experienced farm or mixed vet who is ready for a senior-level opportunity with genuine scope to influence and develop the service, we’d love to hear from you.
